# Thesis Tracker — Alphabet Inc. (GOOGL)
*As of 2026-04-29 · Generated from FinRobot analysis artifacts (Track B: structured thesis snapshot).*
Alphabet delivered a strong fiscal 2025, reporting revenue of approximately $403 billion, representing 15.1% year-over-year growth and accelerating from the 13.9% recorded in 2024. EBITDA reached $180 billion, translating to an EBITDA margin of 44.7%, a meaningful expansion from 38.7% in 2024 and a dramatic recovery from the trough of 30.1% seen in 2022. Earnings per share climbed to $10.91, up from $8.13 the prior year, reflecting both operational leverage and disciplined cost management. Contribution margins have steadily improved, reaching 59.7% in 2025, underscoring the inherent scalability of Alphabet's core advertising and cloud businesses.
